# GIT NOTES (SIMPLE VERSION)

Rule for our project:
master = production (always working, never edit directly)
branch_xxx = your work branch (example: branch_Nov) -> merge into master with a Pull Request

1. ONE-TIME SETUP (only once per computer)

---

git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "you@example.com"

Log in to GitHub from the terminal (a code is shown IN THE TERMINAL, not in email):
gh auth login

2. START A NEW PROJECT (only once per project)

---

git init -b master
git add .
git commit -m "first commit"
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR-NAME/YOUR-REPO.git
git push -u origin master

Create the empty repo on github.com FIRST, otherwise you get "Repository not found".

3. EVERY DAY: WORK ON A BRANCH

---

git switch master # go to master
git pull # get the latest
git switch -c branch_Nov # create + move to your new branch

... write your code ...

git status # what changed?
git add . # pick all changes
git commit -m "add array examples" # save them with a message
git push -u origin branch_Nov # first push of this branch
git push # next pushes of the same branch

4. MERGE INTO MASTER

---

On github.com: open the repo -> "Compare & pull request" -> "Create pull request" -> "Merge pull request".

Then on your computer:
git switch master
git pull # master now has your work

5. CLEAN UP AFTER MERGE

---

git branch -d branch_Nov # delete local branch
git push origin --delete branch_Nov # delete branch on GitHub

6. USEFUL EXTRAS

---

git branch # list local branches (\* = current)
git branch -a # list local + GitHub branches
git log --oneline # short history
git switch branch_Nov # move to another branch

Fix the LAST commit message (only if NOT pushed yet):
git commit --amend -m "new message"

Undo "git add" for one file (keeps your changes):
git restore --staged file.ts

7. .gitignore (files git should NOT save)

---

Create a file named .gitignore in the project root:

node_modules/
.DS_Store
test-results/
playwright-report/

If a file was already committed, stop tracking it (file stays on disk):
git rm --cached .DS_Store
git commit -m "stop tracking .DS_Store"
git push

8. ERRORS WE HIT

---

"fatal: not a git repository" -> run git init first (or cd into the project folder)
"Repository not found" -> create the repo on github.com first, check the URL
"remote origin already exists" -> it is already set; check with git remote -v
"command not found: now" -> you typed a normal sentence in the terminal; only type commands
Cannot delete 'main' on GitHub -> GitHub Settings -> Branches -> change default branch to master first
"master doesn't have my new file" -> the branch is not merged yet; do step 4 (Pull Request) then git pull on master

## QUICK CHEAT SHEET

git switch -c branch_x new branch git add . pick changes
git switch master go to master git commit -m "" save
git pull get latest git push upload
git status what changed git log --oneline history
